# Task 6: Systems of Linear Equations

## 1. Objective
The aim is to solve simultaneous linear equations using NumPy.

## 2. Inputs
The program uses two equations:
2x + y = 8
x + 3y = 13

## 3. Mathematical Operations
The program uses NumPy's `np.linalg.solve()` function to calculate the unknown values of x and y.

## 4. Original Output
The program produces:
x = 2.2
y = 3.6

## 5. Modified Input
I changed the first constant from 8 to 10.

## 6. Observation
Changing the first constant changes the values of x and y.

## 7. Interpretation
NumPy can solve simultaneous equations accurately and efficiently.

## 8. Related Real-World Problem
Businesses can use simultaneous equations to calculate quantities of products sold at different prices.

## 9. Assumptions
The equations have unique solutions, and all coefficients are known.

## 10. New Input Data
The modified equations are:
2x + y = 10
x + 3y = 13

## 11. Output
The modified solution is:
x = 3.4
y = 3.2

## 12. Interpretation of the Modified Problem
The new solutions show how changing a constant affects the unknown values. This method is useful in solving business and engineering problems.